From: panvk-kbase-android worker <panvk-worker@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH csf-v11 022] panvk: BC1-BC7 via GPU compute decode (PANVK_DEBUG=bc_emul)
Generated-by: LLM

Purpose: G615 TEXTURE_FEATURES_0 = 0xc7fe001e, BC mask 0x0001ff80 all zero:
 no BC texturing in HW. Emulate BCn with a GPU compute decode, no CPU decode.
 - BC image = planes[0] raw blocks (LINEAR, used by copies/readback) +
   bc_decoded plane (LINEAR RGBA8/RGBA8_SRGB, RG16 UNORM/SNORM for BC4/5,
   RGBA16F for BC6H) in the same allocation.
 - Sampled views with a BC view format point at bc_decoded with the decoded
   format; BC1_RGB views force A=1 by swizzle. Uncompressed (block-texel)
   views still see the raw plane.
 - vkCmdCopy{Buffer,Memory}ToImage / vkCmdCopyImage into a BC image: raw
   copy, full barrier, then vk_meta compute decode of each dst region
   (SPIR-V decoders in src/panfrost/vulkan/bc, derived from Granite/bcn_layer,
   MIT, Hans-Kristian Arntzen). Image->buffer copies read raw blocks; blits
   sample the decoded plane.
 - Format features: optimal-only SAMPLED|FILTER_LINEAR|MINMAX|BLIT_SRC|
   TRANSFER_SRC|TRANSFER_DST. No linear tiling, DRM modifiers, host image
   copy, storage, attachments, sparse, disjoint or 1D.
 - textureCompressionBC and the 16 BC formats are exposed only with
   PANVK_DEBUG=bc_emul and only when HW lacks BC. Default exposure unchanged.
